{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788270293,"nonce":"Y75Whp5OV9fuYhbLZ2ETLFIfG1g=","message":"NORTH PIN DISCHARGED — `b4d1f04`, 2026-09-01. My previous comment on this issue\nsaid the pin should land here rather than on 3.3 and named it the precondition\nfor module phase. Done, so this issue starts with a coordinate system.\n\n**Row 0 is north**, pinned in `templates/INDEX.md`, stated in `ir.py`'s own\ndocstring so the format declares its orientation instead of leaving it to each\nconsumer, and recorded in DESIGN's decisions log. All three template .md\ndiagrams now say PINNED. North-up was already the convention in `render.py`,\n`CropRenderer` and `map-dump`'s `north_up: true`; only `ir.py` was silent.\n\n\nNot the orientation — the audit. The corpus was checked AGAINST the pin rather\nthan assumed to agree with it, and one template did not:\n\n`freezer-kitchen` carried **`FueledStove_South`**, and `FueledStove` is\n`interactionCellOffset (0,0,-1)`. `Thing.InteractionCell` is\n`Position + offset.RotatedBy(Rotation)`, so `Rot4.South` turns that 180° and\nputs the cook's cell one row NORTH of the stove — row 0, which is a `Wall`.\n**The stove was unusable as drawn.** Now `FueledStove_North`, interaction cell\nrow 2, in the kitchen's own floor. The result is independent of the multi-cell\nanchor convention: corner or centre, same answer, so it did not need pin 1\nsettled first.\n\n\n`INDEX.md` pin 2 documented the rotation suffix as \"the direction the def\nFACES\". That reads perfectly and means **opposite things for different defs**:\na cooler vents toward its rotation (`Cooler_North` vents north — correct), a\nworkbench is used from the side OPPOSITE its rotation (so a stove a cook stands\nsouth of is `Rot4.North`, not South). One gloss, two conventions, and the\ncorpus happened to contain one of each.\n\nPin 2 is now **the `Rot4` value verbatim**, as the game names it and as\n`map-dump` publishes it. A `Rot4` has one meaning and round-trips; a facing is\nprose and belongs in the template's .md. Same rule as `00a1be7`, and as the\n`ToStringHuman` → `ToStringWord` fix that landed the same day on `2a7c064`.\n\nThe audit is complete rather than sampled: `FueledStove` is the ONLY\ninteraction-cell-bearing rotated token in the corpus. `Bed`, `Battery`,\n`Cooler`, `TorchLamp`, `WoodFiredGenerator` and `FirefoamPopper` all leave\n`hasInteractionCell` unset.\n\n\nThe 7x7 module, subdivision vocabulary, shared-wall semantics, the off-phase\nrefusal, and re-cutting or marking the three templates. Nothing here touches\nthose. Two notes for whoever takes it:\n\n- **`Bed` and `Battery` are both size (1,2)** — even on one axis, so\n  `AdjustForRotation`'s even-axis shift applies to them and where they land\n  depends on pin 1 (token = north-west corner) being honoured by\n  `place-layout`'s corner→centre conversion. A 7x7 module is odd on both axes\n  and sidesteps this for whole modules; quarters (3x3) stay odd, halves (7x3)\n  stay odd, but a 2-cell furniture item inside any of them does not.\n- The sequencing in comment #1 is untouched: 3.3's `build` still goes first.","files":null}]}